# idDAS Full Legacy GUI Mock

Run the **unmodified** legacy GUI from `src/` with a vanilla JS mock replacing `/cgi/cmd.lua`.

## Start

```bash
cd mock-client
npm run dev
# http://localhost:8080/target/   ← Topology (MSDH home)
# http://localhost:8080/logs/     ← common pages
```

## Architecture

```
Browser (RequireJS + jQuery + original src/)
  POST /cgi/cmd.lua { cmd: "operators --json" }
       ↓
mock-client/server/devServer.js
       ↓
mockCommandRouter.js  →  fixtures/*.json + in-memory state
```

- **`/target/*`** resolves to `src/msdh/*` or `src/<module>/*` (see `targetResolver.js`)
- **No Lua, no RequireJS changes** — only the CGI endpoint is mocked
- Unknown commands log `[mock-cgi] unhandled command:` — add handlers in `mockCommandRouter.js` + fixtures

## Naming conventions

| Context | Convention | Example |
|---------|------------|---------|
| Legacy DOM `id` | snake_case | `#topology-container` |
| Mock server files | camelCase | `mockCommandRouter.js` |
| Fixture JSON keys | match axsh output | `"Node Type"`, `SysName` |
| Mock commands | exact axsh string | `RFROUTE -o oper1 PROFILES --json` |
| CSS tokens (optional demo) | BEM | `.topology-layer__header` |

## Fixture files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `fixtures/attributes.json` | All GET attributes (tag, mdl, swv, tem, tel, …) |
| `fixtures/operators.json` | operators + USEROPERATOR users |
| `fixtures/topology.json` | sectgrp + topology + racks bundles |
| `fixtures/routing.json` | RFROUTE profiles + route detail + cells |
| `fixtures/alarms.json` | alarms dump --json |
| `fixtures/thresholds.json` | alarmconfig --weblayout |
| `fixtures/system.json` | cellres, connections, measurements, backups, banks |

Unknown commands are handled by catch-all in `defaultHandlers.js` (mutations → `ok`, `--json` → `{}`).

## Adding a new command

1. Add response data to the appropriate fixture JSON
2. Register exact or regex handler in `server/mockCommandRouter.js`
3. Restart dev server; watch terminal for unhandled commands while clicking UI

## Key pages under /target/

| URL | Module |
|-----|--------|
| `/target/` | Topology (`msdh/index.html`) |
| `/target/profiles` | Routing Profiles |
| `/target/status` | Master MSDH status |
| `/target/sectgrp` | BTS Port Management |
| `/target/rfsettings` | RF Management |

Common pages (no `/target/`): `/logs`, `/ethernet`, `/thresholds`, `/inventory`, etc.
